{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Rabbi Moses said: When HaShem is alone, as against all my helpers, I shall look upon my enemies. The meaning is not that HaShem will be one of my helpers; rather, He is as against all the helpers, for when HaShem is my help, I have no need for helpers besides Him. And if I had many helpers and HaShem were not my help — they would not avail me. And this interpretation is lengthy and unnecessary; rather, the meaning is that HaShem will help my helpers and I shall see His vengeance upon my enemies. And because he mentioned that he has helpers, he said that he does not trust in them but in HaShem alone; therefore: it is good to take refuge in HaShem, for in every place He will be a refuge for him. And the meaning: He in whom one takes refuge — He will fight for him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:58.130305395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}